Based on my analysis, the data.json file contains sample advertisement request data that matches the structure of Google Forms submissions used in your project. Here's what it represents:

What is data.json?
The data.json file contains a single advertisement request entry with these fields:

Timestamp: When the request was submitted
Your Name: Contact person's name
Email: Contact email
Phone: Contact phone number
Ad name: Name of the advertisement/company
Ad Description: Description of the advertisement
Amount Willing To Pay: Budget/payment amount
Image: Google Drive link to advertisement image
Company Link: Website/company URL
Why does it exist?
This file appears to be sample/test data that mirrors the structure of Google Forms submissions. Your application integrates with Google Sheets for advertisement requests:

Google Forms → Google Sheets → Your Backend

Users submit advertisement requests via Google Forms
Data gets stored in Google Sheet: "Form Responses 1"
Your backend reads from this sheet using the spreadsheet ID: 1DqAAnv_zjCBraWIzj85lOY_72HxR02OQG-Eb46cPfZU
Field Mapping: The data.json fields directly correspond to what your code expects:

const newAd = new Advertisement({
  name: request['Your Name'],           // Maps to data.json "Your Name"
  email: request.Email,                 // Maps to data.json "Email"  
  phone: request['Phone '],             // Maps to data.json "Phone "
  description: request['Ad Description'], // Maps to data.json "Ad Description"
  adverCompanyName: request['Ad name'], // Maps to data.json "Ad name"
  // etc.
});